{"id":"word:hebrew:H3680","type":"word","title":"כָּסָה","subtitle":"H3680 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, to plump , i.e. fill up hollows; by implication, to cover (for clothing or secrecy)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כָּסָה (H3680) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 153 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כָּסָה (kâçâh) means properly, to plump , i.e. fill up hollows; by implication, to cover (for clothing or secrecy) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 21 16."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כָּסָה","transliteration":"kâçâh","pronunciation":"kaw-saw'","strong":"H3680","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3680","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["הַֽ/מְכַסֶּ֣ה","לְ/כַסּ֗וֹת","וַ/תְּכַ֖ס","כִּסָּה","לְ/כַסּ֥וֹת"],"morphs":[["HR/Vpc",12],["HVpp3ms",10],["HVpi3ms",9],["HTd/Vprmsa",8],["HC/Vpw3fs",6],["HC/Vpw3ms",5],["HVpp1cs",5],["HC/Vpq3cp",5],["HC/Vpw3mp",4],["HVpp3fs",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, to plump , i.e. fill up hollows; by implication, to cover (for clothing or secrecy)","usage":"clad self, close, clothe, conceal, cover (self), (flee to) hide, overwhelm. Compare 3780 .","full":"H3680. kasah I. [ כָּסָה ] verb cover (Late Hebrew כָּסָה Pi; Aramaic כְּסָא chiefly Pa; Pa`el hide, cover ; covering , garment ; Arabic () clothe , garment ; Assyrian kusû , cover: kusîtu , garment Dl HWB 342 ) — Qal , only Participle active כֹּסֶה ; — 1 conceal shame Prov 12:16 ; knowledge 12:23 . 2 passive (construct) חֲטָאָה כְּסוּי Psa 32:1 covered in respect of sin (by God, which he thus puts out of sight) (|| נְשׂוּימֶּֿשַׁע ). Niph`al Perfect 3feminine singular נִכְסָ֑תָּה , covered , with waves Jer 51:42 ; Infinitive construct הִכָּסוֺת Ezek 24:8 , (blood) not to be covered. Pi`el Perfect 3masculine singular כִּסָּה Num 9:15 12 t.; suffix כִּסָּהוּ Lev 17:13 ; Num 17:7 ; כִּסָּמוֺ Exod 15:10 ; 3 feminine singular כִּסְּתָה Gen 38:15 5 t.; 1 singular כִּסִּיתִי Psa 32:5 3 t.; כִּסֵּתִי Ezek 31:15 (strike out Co); כִּסֵּיתִי 32:7 13 t. Perfect; Imperfect 3masculine singular יְכַסֶּה Isa 6:2 8 t.; וַיְכַס Exod 10:15 4 t.; suffix יְכַסֶּ֑דָּ Hab 2:17 ; יְכַסֶּנָּה Ezek 30:18 ; 3 masculine plural suffix יְכַסְיֻמוּ Exod 15:5 41t. Imperfect; Imperative suffix כַּסּוּנוּ Hosea 10:8 ; Infinitive construct כַּסּוֺת Mal 2:13 11 t.; כַּסֹּת Num 4:15 ; suffix כַּסֹּתוֺ Exod 26:13 ; Participle מְכַסֶּה Prov 10:18 12 t.; plural מְכַסִּים Isa 11:9 ; feminine plural מְכַסּוֺת Ezek 1:11 , 23 (twice in verse); &#8212; 1 cover, clothe Judg 4:19 ; Ezek 16:10 (2 accusative), 16:18 ; Jonah 3:6 is apparently reflexive, with accusative of garment (strange; read perhaps וַיִּכָּס ); nakedness Gen 9:23 (J), Exod 28:42 (P), Ezek 16:8 ; Hosea 2:11 ; the naked Isa 58:7 ; Ezek 18:7 , 16 (+ accusative of thing); the face and legs of seraphim Isa 6:2 (twice in verse); bodies of cherubim Ezek 1:11 , 23 (twice in verse); the face Gen 38:15 (J), Ezek 12:6 , 12 , figurative Job 23:17 ; earth with the great deep Psa 104:6 ; heavens with glory Hab 3:3 ; with בְּ of the clothing Gen 38:14 (J), Deut 22:12 , these two apparently reflexive, compare Jonah 3:6 above; Judg 4:18 ; 1Kin 1:1 ; heaven with clouds Psa 147:8 , with glory Ezek 32:7 . 2 cover, conceal blood Gen 37:26 (J), Job 16:18 ; human ordure Deut 23:14 ; mountains conceal men from God Hosea 10:8 ; cover transgressions Job 31:33 ; Prov 17:9 ; 28:13 ; iniquity Psa 32:5 ; righteousness 40:11 ; hatred Prov 10:18 ; a thing 11:13 ; face of judge so that he cannot see justice Job 9:24 ; rulers and seers Isa 29:10 ; with בְּ of covering Lev 17:13 (H), 1Sam 19:13 ; face by fat Job 15:27 ; sun by a cloud Ezek 32:7 ; with מִן from whom Gen 18:17 (J), Job 33:17 . 3 cover (with covering of protection), a pit Exod 21:33 (Covt. code); with cloud of incense, the Kapporeth Lev 16:13 (P); coverings of the sacred tent, tabernacle, and their furniture Exod 26:13 ; Num 4:9 , 15 (P); with בְּ of the covering 4:5 , 8 , 11 , 12 (P); Zion יָדִי בְּצֵל Isa 51:16 . 4 cover, spread over , fat, the inwards Exod 29:13 , 22 ; Lev 3:3 , 9 , 14 ; 4:8 (with עַל ), 7:3 (P); leprosy, the skin and flesh 13:12-13 , (P); the cloud of the theophany, the mount Exod 24:15-16 , (P), the tent of meeting 40:34 ; Num 17:7 (P), and the tabernacle 9:15-16 , (P); altar with tears Mal 2:13 (2 accusative); Jerusalem with multitude of camels Isa 60:6 ; of handiwork 1Kin 7:18 , 41 , 42 2Chr 4:12-13 ,. 5 cover, overwhelm , followed by accusative, the sea the Egyptians Exod 14:28 (P), 15:5 , 10 (song), Josh 24:7 (E), Psa 78:53 ; 106:11 ; waters Job 22:11 ; 38:34 ; Psa 104:9 ; Jer 46:8 ; Ezek 26:19 ; locusts the eye of the land Exod 10:5 , 15 (J), also Israel Num 22:5 , 11 (J); frogs the land Exod 8:2 (P); quails the camp 16:13 (P); cloud the land Ezek 30:18 ; 38:9 , 16 ; darkness the earth Isa 60:2 ; dust a city Ezek 26:10 ; the depths of the sea by God Job 36:30 ; with a reference to a person's shame Psa 44:16 ; 69:8 ; Jer 51:51 ; Obadiah 10; Micah 7:10 ; horror Psa 55:6 ; Ezek 7:18 ; violence Prov 10:6 , 11 ; Hab 2:17 ; confusion Jer 3:25 ; mischief Psa 140:10 ; God covers sin 85:3 (|| עון נשׂא ), compare 32:1 (Qal). 6 followed by על of person or thing covered, cover over: cherubim over the ark 2Chr 5:8 ; over the dead, the earth Num 16:33 (JE), Psa 106:17 ; Isa 26:21 , worms Job 21:26 ; dust over blood Ezek 24:7 ; waters over the sea Hab 2:14 , compare לַיָּם Isa 11:9 ; (see Dr § 135. 7 Obs. ); love covereth over all sins Prov 10:12 ; God covereth over iniquity Nehemiah 3:37; people not to cover over a guilty person Deut 13:9 ; + accusative of object covering (Da Synt. § 75 ), figurative covering over the garment with violence Mal 2:16 ; God's hands with light Job 36:32 ; + בְּ of covering Psa 44:20 . Note. — כִסִּתִי אֵלֶיךָ) ( Psa 143:9 is error for חָסִיתִי according to ᵐ5 κατέφυγον SS, but חסה not construct with אֶלֿ ; חִכִּיתִי Bae; אֶתתְּֿהוֺם עָלָיו כִּסֵּתִי הֶאֱבַלְ